  "prefLabel": "En 1016.03 Grievance Resolution Process",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1016.03 Grievance Resolution Process. If a resolution is not reached in 10 business days from the date of the notice of dispute, the following shall be available:\n\n(a) A party may request in writing to continue negotiations for an additional 25 business days;\n\n(b) The applicant may file an informal complaint with the department’s consumer services division and request a conference to attempt to resolve the dispute; and\n\n(c) Within 10 business days of a request for continued negotiations or within 10 business days of the conference referenced in (b) above in this section, the applicant and the utility shall each provide a written description of technical and regulatory details relevant to the dispute. Nothing shall prevent the parties from continuing informal negotiations if a department-attended conference is requested.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
